4.2 Important database rules
The developer must implement the following:
1. Every asset must belong to exactly one organisation.
2. Every asset must have a unique internal identifier within its organisation.
3. Every movement must reference an existing asset.
4. The previous location must match the asset's current location when the movement is completed.
5. The new location must be valid and active.
6. Completed movements must have a completion timestamp and responsible user.
7. Rejected movements must retain their rejection reason.
8. Historical assignments must remain available.
9. Asset records must not be physically deleted when they have historical transactions.
10. All organisation-owned records must be protected by organisation-level access restrictions.
One further technical refinement: A movement transaction should update the current location and movement history atomically. PostgreSQL transactions and appropriate concurrency controls should be used to prevent conflicting transfers.

