The application should be built as a modular monolith initially, rather than a collection of separate microservices.

This means the different functions are logically separated in the code, but deployed as one main backend application.

It is less complicated to build, test, maintain and deploy at the initial stage. Individual services can be separated later if usage justifies it.
5.2 Why I recommend Django
Django is particularly appropriate for this project because it provides:
- Built-in user authentication.
- Database management through its ORM.
- Administrative interfaces.
- Data validation.
- Permission management.
- Database migration support.
- Security protections.
Django REST Framework will allow the frontend to communicate with the backend through APIs.

Next.js will provide the user-facing application.

