10. Features and activities deliberately excluded from this project
Since you have asked that subscriptions be left out, I am removing the entire commercial subscription and billing component from the current specification.

The following will not be part of the initial project:
Excluded component	Reason
Subscription plans	Not required at this stage
Monthly or annual billing	Not required at this stage
Payment gateway	No payment collection required
Customer subscription dashboard	Outside current scope
Automated renewals	Outside current scope
Subscription invoices	Outside current scope
Payment reminders	Outside current scope
GPS hardware tracking	Not part of the initial asset-tracking model
Full accounting module	Separate business function
Procurement management	Separate business function

The application may still have a platform administrator who can manage accounts and provide technical support. That is an administrative function, not subscription management.

I would also avoid introducing financial depreciation and complex asset valuation in the first release. Basic acquisition cost can be recorded, but accounting calculations should be a later module.

11. Testing and acceptance criteria
This is one of the most important additions to the revised proposal.

Before considering AssetTrack ready, the developer must demonstrate that the following tests pass.
Test	Expected result
Register a new asset	Asset is saved with a unique ID
Register two identical items	Both receive different IDs
Register without a category	System rejects incomplete entry
Register without a location	System rejects incomplete entry
Scan an asset QR code	Correct asset record opens
Submit a movement request	Movement is recorded as pending where approval is required
Reject a movement	Current location remains unchanged
Complete a movement	Current location updates correctly
Move the same asset twice	Both transactions appear in history
Submit a duplicate transfer	System detects the location conflict
Search an asset	Correct asset is retrieved
Filter by location	Only matching assets are displayed
Report a missing asset	Missing status and investigation record are created
Assign an asset	Responsibility is recorded
Archive an asset	Asset history remains available
Access another organisation's data	Access is denied
Export asset register	Report matches the underlying records

I would additionally require:
- Database backup restoration testing.
- Permission testing for every user role.
- Concurrent movement testing.
- Validation of all date and time records.
- Testing of Excel imports with duplicate and incomplete rows.
The most important acceptance test is whether the application can correctly establish the current location of an asset after multiple movements, including rejected, cancelled and completed transactions.

12. Project implementation roadmap
I recommend the following development sequence.
Stage	Activities	Deliverable
1. Requirements	Confirm features, user roles and business rules	Approved SRS
2. System design	Database, architecture and interface designs	Technical design document
3. Backend	Database, authentication and APIs	Functional backend
4. Frontend	Dashboard, forms and management screens	Functional web interface
5. Integration	Connect frontend, backend and database	Integrated application
6. Testing	Functional, security and user acceptance testing	Tested MVP
7. Deployment	Hosting, backups and production configuration	Live application
8. Pilot	Introduce the application to selected users	Pilot evaluation report

A realistic development schedule should be agreed after the requirements and interface designs are approved. The duration will depend on the development team, available resources and complexity of implementation.
12.1 Pilot testing
I recommend testing the initial product with:
- One household.
- Two schools.
- One office.
- One hotel.
This will establish whether the system works across different environments.

The pilot should measure:
1. Accuracy of asset registration.
2. Accuracy of current-location information.
3. Percentage of movements recorded.
4. Time required to complete an asset audit.
5. Ease of use.
6. Accuracy of generated reports.
7. User satisfaction.
8. Frequency of system errors.
The pilot should also identify which features are genuinely useful and which ones can be removed or simplified.

